Subject: [PATCH] Track completed OUTPUT writes independently of capture history

The allocated-buffer ring also preserves capture-frame history. It is not an
OUTPUT completion queue: returning its first entry can dequeue an unsubmitted
buffer, and rotating it can return one completion more than once. Track the
pending completion under list_lock without changing the capture position map.
Wake empty blocking OUTPUT dequeues on STREAMOFF; report MMAP poll readiness
only for pending output. Keep write(2) and capture polling semantics intact.

Related upstream investigation: https://github.com/v4l2loopback/v4l2loopback/pull/656
This is a separate minimal candidate, not an assertion that that PR was merged.
Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/v4l2loopback.c
+++ b/v4l2loopback.c
@@ -326,6 +326,9 @@
 /* struct keeping state and settings of loopback device */
 
 struct v4l2l_buffer {
+	/* Under list_lock: a written OUTPUT buffer not yet returned by DQBUF.
+	 * Separate from list_head, which also retains capture-frame history. */
+	bool output_pending;
 	struct v4l2_buffer buffer;
 	struct list_head list_head;
 	atomic_t use_count;
@@ -1608,7 +1611,8 @@
